  "steps": [
    "Mix the dough ingredients in a stand mixer in the order listed, then knead on low for 15 minutes. Cover and proof 75-90 minutes until doubled.",
    "Make the filling: heat the oil in a wok and stir-fry the shallots 1 minute. Add the sugar, light soy sauce, oyster sauce, sesame oil, and dark soy sauce and stir until bubbling. Add the chicken stock and flour and cook until thickened, then stir in the pork. Cool.",
    "Knead the dough 5 minutes, divide into 16 pieces, roll each into a circle, fill, and pinch closed.",
    "Let the buns rise 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 400°F. Brush with egg wash and sprinkle with sesame seeds.",
    "Put the buns in the oven and immediately lower it to 350°F. Bake 22-25 minutes until golden, then brush with the sugar syrup while hot."
  ],
